Z||000000||KnightRyder31||04-28-2000||02:13 PM||||My check engine light comes on sometimes(not to often) but it only stays on for about 30 secs. Also, when I'm at a red light, I think my car idles way to low....at like 600RPM. Is that the problem?||||reg||5
Z||000001||triker||04-28-2000||02:25 PM||||Once the light comes on, even if it goes off again, it sets a code in the ECM.  You'll have to retrieve the code and go from there.  If you don't know how to retrieve the code, E-mail me and I'll tell you how.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lennyb4||04-28-2000||02:31 PM||||Knightrider im not sure where you live but if theres an Auto-Zone near you they will give you a jumper to read your ECM with (just a cheap piece of steel) but it works well. If not then you could always use a paper clip or a short piece of wire to do the job.Then just refer to either Haynes or Chiltons manuals for the code.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||04-28-2000||02:51 PM||||Yea,I live 10mins from autozone. I live in Michigan. Triker, I will email you sometime. But what about the low RPM at a stop....could that be the prob? Someone once told me that the light probably had to do with the EGR. And other than the low RPM's, and a gurgeling noise at high RPM's....there isnt anything wrong that I could point out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||04-28-2000||05:21 PM||||I'm gonna guess your light flashes the IAC code (sorry, don't remember the numbers).<P>Basically it does this if the idle varies more than 50 rpm over a specified period of time. This usually occurs as a result of a vacuum leak, but other things could result in this code.<P>And it's possible that a new IAC won't fix the problem, for the reasons discussed above.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||04-29-2000||05:10 AM||||Here you go KnightRyder31 <A HREF="http://www.syty.org/d&e.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.syty.org/d&e.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||04-29-2000||11:03 AM||||Hey deceler, my RPM is below what its supost to be. 500RPM at a full stop(Not in park, just with the brake down) It only is above when I'm in park, then sometimes it skys to 2,000+ RPM's. Well, I dont know the prob, so if you can tell me....please do so.<BR>-----Knight-----<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 04-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||04-30-2000||11:16 AM||||Usually vacuum leaks result in the IAC code flashing the check engine light for 30 seconds or so...but a leak would cause a lot higher idle than you're experiencing.<P>Could in fact be the IAC, could even be retarded timing. I'd suggest getting a cheap Chilton or Haynes manual...it covers how to locate codes and what they mean. Or you could probably find this same info on the board by searching for it.<P>Wasn't "Knight Ryder" the talking Trans-Am driven by David Hasselhoff ?||||reg||1
